{
  "an3.57:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 3.57 ",
  "an3.57:0.2": "6. Brahmins ",
  "an3.57:0.3": "With Vacchagotta ",
  "an3.57:1.1": "Then the wanderer Vacchagotta went up to the Buddha, and exchanged greetings with him. ",
  "an3.57:1.2": "When the greetings and polite conversation were over, he sat down to one side and said to the Buddha: ",
  "an3.57:1.3": "“I have heard, worthy Gotama, that the ascetic Gotama says this: ",
  "an3.57:1.4": "‘Gifts should only be given to me, not to others. ",
  "an3.57:1.5": "Gifts should only be given to my disciples, not to the disciples of others. ",
  "an3.57:1.6": "Only what is given to me is very fruitful, not what is given to others. ",
  "an3.57:1.7": "Only what is given to my disciples is very fruitful, not what is given to the disciples of others.’ ",
  "an3.57:1.8": "",
  "an3.57:1.9": "",
  "an3.57:1.10": "",
  "an3.57:1.11": "",
  "an3.57:1.12": "",
  "an3.57:1.13": "I trust those who say this repeat what the worthy Gotama has said, and do not misrepresent him with an untruth? Is their explanation in line with the teaching? Are there any legitimate grounds for rebuttal and criticism? ",
  "an3.57:1.14": "For we don’t want to misrepresent the worthy Gotama.” ",
  "an3.57:2.1": "“Vaccha, those who say this ",
  "an3.57:2.2": "",
  "an3.57:2.3": "",
  "an3.57:2.4": "",
  "an3.57:2.5": "do not repeat what I have said. They misrepresent me with what is false and untrue. ",
  "an3.57:2.6": "Anyone who prevents another from giving makes an obstacle and a roa